# Every text file is LF on every checkout, including a checkout on Windows.
# Git for Windows writes CRLF by default. See dbmeta D89 and D110.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The reference images, the test fonts and the test files of upstream are
# copies of the files of upstream, byte for byte (docs/UPSTREAM.md). Git must
# not change them. An SVG file of a test can hold CRLF line ends on purpose.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.svgz binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
testdata/** -text
svg/testdata/** -text
internal/*/testdata/** -text
